/*
class Node {
    int data;
    Node next;

    Node(int d) {
        data = d;
        next = null;
    }
}*/

class Solution {
    public boolean isPalindrome(Node head) {

        ArrayDeque<Integer> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();            // O(n) space for stack
        
                                                                    // Pass 1: Push all node values onto stack (builds reverse order)
        for (Node cur = head; cur != null; cur = cur.next) {       // Traverse: head → tail
            stack.push(cur.data);                                  // LIFO: top = last node
        }
        
                                                                    // Pass 2: Compare each node with stack's top (reverse comparison)
        for (Node cur = head; cur != null; cur = cur.next) {       // Traverse: head → tail
            if (stack.pop() != cur.data) {                         // Pop: tail → head
                return false;                                      // Mismatch → NOT palindrome
            }
        }
        
        return true;                                               // All matched → IS palindrome
    }
}

//////////////////////// DRY RUN /////////////////////////////

Example 1: 1 -> 2 -> 1 -> 1 -> 2 -> 1  (Palindrome ✓)

--------------------------------- PASS 1: BUILD STACK ---------------------------------

cur = 1  →  stack.push(1)  →  stack: [1]
cur = 2  →  stack.push(2)  →  stack: [2, 1]
cur = 1  →  stack.push(1)  →  stack: [1, 2, 1]
cur = 1  →  stack.push(1)  →  stack: [1, 1, 2, 1]
cur = 2  →  stack.push(2)  →  stack: [2, 1, 1, 2, 1]
cur = 1  →  stack.push(1)  →  stack: [1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 1]  ← TOP

Stack (Top→Bottom): 1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 1


--------------------------------- PASS 2: COMPARE ---------------------------------

cur=1, stack.pop()=1  →  1 == 1  ✓
cur=2, stack.pop()=2  →  2 == 2  ✓
cur=1, stack.pop()=1  →  1 == 1  ✓
cur=1, stack.pop()=1  →  1 == 1  ✓
cur=2, stack.pop()=2  →  2 == 2  ✓
cur=1, stack.pop()=1  →  1 == 1  ✓

All matched → Return TRUE ✓


--------------------------------- VISUAL ---------------------------------

Original:  1 → 2 → 1 → 1 → 2 → 1
           ↓  ↓  ↓  ↓  ↓  ↓
Stack:     1  2  1  1  2  1  (pops in reverse: 1,2,1,1,2,1)

Reverse:   1 → 2 → 1 → 1 → 2 → 1  (same as original)
           ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓  ✓


